# config/teleop_v2.env — v2-only defaults, sourced by run_teleop_v2.sh after
# config/teleop.env. Everything the two launchers share stays in that file;
# only the DexPilot settings live here.
#
# As always: environment wins over this file, command line flags win over both.

# The MANUS teleop checkout that owns the retargeting core, the V6 Force URDF
# and the tuned DexPilot configs (src/v6f_teleop, urdf/v6_force, configs/*.yml).
# retargeting_node_v2.py reads it as $V6F_TELEOP_ROOT.
V6F_TELEOP_ROOT="${V6F_TELEOP_ROOT:-$HOME/v6f_manuse_teleoperation/V6_Teleoperation}"

# The interpreter the retargeting node runs on. It needs dex_retargeting and
# pinocchio (numpy 2.x); this repo's .venv is pinned to numpy 1.x for mediapipe,
# so the two cannot be the same one.
RETARGET_PY="${RETARGET_PY:-$V6F_TELEOP_ROOT/.venv/bin/python}"

# Operator hand size, as the robot's finger length over the operator's, knuckle
# to pad centre. Empty measures it from the first $CALIBRATE frames of the
# session, which is what you want with MediaPipe: its world landmarks are metric
# only approximately, and the error is per-person.
#
# Set it to a number to pin it instead — useful when comparing two runs, since a
# value that measures itself is not the value you wrote down. 1.6 is the
# MANUS project's measured figure, in the middle of a plateau running from about
# 1.5 to beyond 2.2 where every pinch stays inside half a millimetre.
SCALING="${SCALING:-}"
CALIBRATE="${CALIBRATE:-150}"

# DexPilot's output low-pass, overriding the config's 0.25. It is an EMA on the
# solved joints stepped **once per camera frame**, so its lag is (1-a)/a frames:
# at this machine's 30 fps camera, 0.25 costs 100 ms of group delay (300 ms to
# 90% of a step) and 0.6 costs 22 ms (100 ms to 90%). Measured, not estimated.
#
# It is the largest single delay in the chain, so raise this first when the hand
# feels sluggish. Empty keeps the config's 0.25. Lower it again if the fingers
# start to jitter — the filter is also what hides MediaPipe's per-frame noise.
RETARGET_ALPHA="${RETARGET_ALPHA:-}"

# The producers mirror the camera image for the operator (cv2.flip), which hands
# MediaPipe a mirrored hand. 'true' negates x to put the chirality back. Flip it
# to false only if the robot thumb opposes towards the wrong side; the node also
# warns on its own when the tracked hand's chirality disagrees with the loaded
# hand model.
UNDO_MIRROR="${UNDO_MIRROR:-true}"
